  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWhile slow to completely clear the area, high pressure and dry air \nare working together to scatter the remaining clouds across the \nScioto Valley and west-central Ohio this afternoon. Some high clouds \nare possible overnight, but conditions will primarily be clear. This \nprovides a favorable opportunity for fog development. River valleys \nand lower terrain will be the most susceptible, however, the longer \nnights this time of year should allow for fog to spread over rural \nareas as well. Conditions improve throughout the morning hours.\n\nDominant high pressure persists over the Ohio Valley through the end\nof the week. Temperatures warm to above seasonal normals with 60s\noccurring Wednesday through Saturday. \n\nA weak upper level disturbance over the Gulf will combine with a \ntrough moving through the Midwest late in the weekend to provide the\nnext potential for rainfall across the area. Some of this rainfall\nmay reach the area late Saturday, but timing differences exist with\nthe disturbance to the south of the region. Confidence is a bit\nhigher on Sunday with a passing cold front.",
